-- Purpose: Handles Legendary Car Shop logic. Strictly crafting system, persistent timers, sacrifice mechanics.
-- Purpose: Handles Mythical Car Shop logic. Strictly crafting system, persistent timers, sacrifice mechanics.
-- Runs on: Server
-- Location: ServerScriptService > MythicalShopService
-- Dependencies: ReplicatedStorage.CarStats, ServerStorage.MythicalCraftingInventoryFunction, TycoonDataHandler
-- Public API: None (Event/Bindable driven)
-- Networking: ShopRemotes.MythicalShop.{RequestOpenShop, OpenShopUI, MythicalShopUpdate, GetMythicalShopState, CraftMythicalCar, SacrificeMythicalIngredient}
-- Security: Server authority on cash, exact inventory checks, exact timer tracking.
-- Notes: Uses exact timer duration (Yamura=12h, LaRossa=48h) and exact ingredient requirement list.
--
-- FIX: Removed the Players.PlayerRemoving listener from this script.
--
--   ROOT CAUSE OF THE PROGRESS-WIPE BUG:
--   Both TycoonDataHandler and MythicalShopService connected to PlayerRemoving.
--   Roblox fires all PlayerRemoving listeners concurrently, so the data handler's
--   save() would call PersistenceBindable:Invoke("Get", player) at the exact same
--   moment this script ran PlayerSessions[uid] = nil. getSession() would then find
--   no session, create a blank one, and return {} — causing the data handler to
--   faithfully save empty CraftProgress, wiping all sacrifice progress on every leave.
--
--   THE FIX:
--   The "Close" action inside PersistenceBindable.OnInvoke already performs the
--   same cleanup (PlayerSessions[uid] = nil). The data handler calls "Close" AFTER
--   calling "Get", guaranteeing the correct order:
--     1. save() calls "Get"  → returns real session data      ✅
--     2. save() calls "Close" → session cleaned up             ✅
--   Removing the competing PlayerRemoving listener lets that contract hold.

